# Conformance probe pack for gate blocks (spec 0.17) at the end of the input
# and the encoded length. Fixed `bits` layout, least significant bit first.
# Public. No kinds. One byte per word. Exercises: a gate beyond the input does
# not hold, and neither does its `!` form; a field of a held block beyond the
# input is `malformed-wire` unless it is `optional`; a gate that holds on
# zero bits holds on encode wherever it lies (step 4: bits nothing wrote
# read 0), so a block that is not open is held, writes its sentinel and
# extends the output; an `optional` line of a held block counts toward the
# encoded length.
#
#   byte 0       x, outside any block
#   byte 1       the gate of y and z: they are there when the byte is 0
#   byte 2       y, absent 255
#   byte 3       z, optional
#   byte 4       the gate of w: w is there when the byte is not 0
#   byte 5       w
format     conformance-gates-edge
version    0.17.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
field   probe.x   0:0:8    uint
if      0:8:8  0
  field probe.y   0:16:8   uint  absent 255
  field probe.z   0:24:8   uint  optional
end
if      !0:32:8 0
  field probe.w   0:40:8   uint
end
